# Cross-frame DivByZero propagation (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1c): a
# division by zero raised INSIDE a callee (`q`) propagates to a
# `catch Fault.DivByZero` in its DIRECT caller (`main`), without unwind — the
# callee writes the DivByZero fault tag into a hidden trailing slot, and the
# caller reads the tag and dispatches to the handler before reading the result.
# Expected stdout: 999 (the handler value), NOT a panic.
int q(int a, int b): a / b                # may div0; NO local catch

void main():
    int z = 0
    int r = q(10, z) catch Fault.DivByZero: 999
    print(f"{r}")
